{
  "id": "clerambaults-syndrome",
  "term": "Clérambault’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Clérambault’s syndrome, also called erotomania, is a rare delusional disorder in which a person persistently believes that someone else, often a person of higher social or professional status, is in love with them despite little or no real contact. It commonly includes intense infatuation and attributing the person’s own feelings or intentions to the supposed admirer.",
